From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:00:41 +0000
Subject: irqchip/mips-gic: fix local timer/perfctr/fdc on single-cluster
 systems

Commit d1cb1437b785 ("irqchip/mips-gic: Prevent indirect access to
clusters without CPU cores") added early returns to
gic_mask_local_irq_all_vpes() and gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes(), and
an "if (multicluster)" guard around the vo_map iteration in
gic_irq_domain_map(), so that single-cluster systems skip the
multi-cluster redirect-block iteration.

A single-cluster system still needs its local VPE's vl_smask, vl_rmask
and vl_map programmed, and now nothing does it. gic_cpu_startup() runs
before request_irq(), so cd->map and cd->mask are still zero when
gic_all_vpes_irq_cpu_online() programs the boot VPE; after request_irq()
the unmask path returns immediately and never touches the local smask.
The interrupt stays masked for good. With the timer that means
calibrate_delay() spins forever on a jiffy that never arrives.

The precondition is that the local interrupt is routed through the GIC
domain at all. gic_get_c0_compare_int() returns the plain CP0 interrupt
when gic_local_irq_is_routable(GIC_LOCAL_INT_TIMER) is false, and that
is the common case, which is why the regression has not been widely
reported: only a single-cluster part whose GIC does route the local
timer, performance counter or FDC reaches this code.

Restore the local-VPE register writes on single-cluster systems while
preserving the multi-cluster redirect-block path, and populate cd->map
and cd->mask unconditionally so secondary VPEs pick the correct state up
from gic_all_vpes_irq_cpu_online() on their later cpu-online transition.

Fixes: d1cb1437b785 ("irqchip/mips-gic: Prevent indirect access to clusters without CPU cores")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
index 19a57c5e2b2e..d9405c7dfff2 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
@@ -512,13 +512,22 @@ static void gic_mask_local_irq_all_vpes(struct irq_data *d)
 	struct gic_all_vpes_chip_data *cd;
 	int intr, cpu;
 
-	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus())
-		return;
-
 	intr = GIC_HWIRQ_TO_LOCAL(d->hwirq);
 	cd = irq_data_get_irq_chip_data(d);
 	cd->mask = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * Single-cluster systems must still mask the IRQ on the currently
+	 * executing VPE; secondary VPEs pick the new mask state up via
+	 * gic_all_vpes_irq_cpu_online() as they come online. Multi-cluster
+	 * systems iterate to push the mask to all online VPEs through the
+	 * GIC redirect block.
+	 */
+	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus()) {
+		write_gic_vl_rmask(BIT(intr));
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for_each_online_cpu_gic(cpu, &gic_lock)
 		write_gic_vo_rmask(BIT(intr));
 }
@@ -528,13 +537,15 @@ static void gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes(struct irq_data *d)
 	struct gic_all_vpes_chip_data *cd;
 	int intr, cpu;
 
-	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus())
-		return;
-
 	intr = GIC_HWIRQ_TO_LOCAL(d->hwirq);
 	cd = irq_data_get_irq_chip_data(d);
 	cd->mask = true;
 
+	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus()) {
+		write_gic_vl_smask(BIT(intr));
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for_each_online_cpu_gic(cpu, &gic_lock)
 		write_gic_vo_smask(BIT(intr));
 }
@@ -701,6 +712,13 @@ static int gic_irq_domain_map(struct irq_domain *d, unsigned int virq,
 	if (mips_cps_multicluster_cpus()) {
 		for_each_online_cpu_gic(cpu, &gic_lock)
 			write_gic_vo_map(mips_gic_vx_map_reg(intr), map);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * On single-cluster systems gic_cpu_startup() runs on the
+		 * boot CPU only, so a secondary released by firmware never
+		 * unmasks its own local interrupts.
+		 */
+		write_gic_vl_map(mips_gic_vx_map_reg(intr), map);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
